==Trivia==
*Even though his and [[Project A]]'s Japanese names can both be translated as "Master", they aren't quite the same: Master A. is 師匠 ''Shishō'', which is closer to "instructor", while Project A is 巨匠 ''Kyoshō'', meaning "master of an art/craft".
*Master A. and his variants' Japanese descriptions follow a theme of having dark thoughts and schemes that they often fail to execute one way or the other.
**[[Professor A.]] is a sensual novelist known for a work that describes a girl's puberty, though much like Master A. he has no experience dating women whatsoever. In the Korean version, he is even stated to be on the way to becoming a wizard (the Internet slang term "wizard" refers to a virgin over the age of 30).
**[[Project A]] is an artist who creates nude paintings by acquiring inspiration from others via contact before using his tongue to paint. That said, he was never able to find a model for his works.
**Similar to Project A, [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]] is also an artist, though he creates sculptures instead. He made a pact with the [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] for X-ray vision, ostensibly to create nude sculptures, which backfired horribly as it only enables him to see skeletons, ruining his ability to sculpt.
*Master A.'s tail is unusually short compared to real anteaters, whose tails are almost as long as their bodies.
*Despite being the fourth [[Stories of Legend]] enemy encountered, Master A. has the lowest ID out of all of them, which suggests that the first thing [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]] set out to do when creating new enemies for [[Legend Stages]] was ensure [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] wouldn't be the answer to everything.

